{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/998602-mage-virtue-vice-replacements","id":998602,"title":"Mage Virtue/Vice Replacements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T21:07:52-07:00","id":998602,"title":"Mage Virtue/Vice Replacements","content":"I understand that Mages are arguably the most fundamentally human Splat out there, and that's why they maintain most of the same Anchors, but I still think it feels a little odd that people who brushed up against the glorious and terrible Platonic truths of the cosmos wouldn't be fundamentally changed in their mindset. This is a small hack to correct that.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Truth: The Touch of the Supernal</span></b><br /> <br /> When a Mage Awakens, she has revealed to her many fundamental Truths of reality. Much like how certain objects in the Fallen World resonate most with specific Platonic forms, a nascent Mage's soul resonates most clearly with one specific Truth, which leaves an indelible mark on her soul. This fundamental part of her being acts to center her as she lives in the Fallen, and provides her with strength and direction.<br /> <br /> When a Mage experiences her Truth clearly reflected in the Fallen or acts upon it in a minor way, she regains a point of Mana or a point of Willpower, as her soul is invigorated by this fleeting touch of the Supernal in her life.<br /> <br /> When a Mage acts upon her Truth in a grandiose fashion, or acts on her Truth at material risk to herself, she replenishes all her Willpower instead, the energy of the Supernal washing over her and restoring her strength and focus.<br /> <br /> She can also use her Truth as a Yantra (+2), provided she is specifically casting a spell that reflects her Truth, or with the explicit intent of enacting her Truth in the Fallen World. Acting on a Truth also provides a bonus for rolls with Breaking Points in service of that Truth.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Truths:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Never Too Late to Change:</b> Howard Awakened when he was at rock bottom, strung out on whatever drug was cheap enough for him to get his hands on and plentiful enough to OD on. He thought he was dying when the Demons dragged him to the Iron Gauntlet and had him write his name, but when they let him go, he thought at first that God had spared him. When he woke up, he saw the filthy alley he had been passed out in, and just, <i>stood up</i>. He cleaned himself up, got a job at a Subway, and managed to stay clean ever since. When he's not making the fastest damn Chicken Bacon Ranch you ever saw, he's in the thick of things, trying to help all the people still struggling, the people he used to be. If they're still breathing, they still have a chance, after all.<br /> <b>Regain Mana or Willpower:</b> When Howard provides moral support to somebody in a difficult time or sees somebody earnestly resolve to turn their life around.<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower:</b> When Howard puts his well-being at risk to help redeem someone.<br /> <b>Use As Yantra:</b> When attempting to free others from their inner demons.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunt or be Hunted:</b> Nadia didn't quite understand what happened to her that night, when she fought off that mugger. No, &quot;fought&quot; isn't quite right. The thief never stood a chance. One moment, he was looming over her like some formless predator ready to pounce, and the next moment, Nadia reared up and pounced first. She broke his leg and dislocated his shoulder, and he never knew what hit him. Her hand still wet from the blood pouring from his busted, crooked nose, she left a print on the wall, a pact signed in her first prey's blood with the Primal Wild. Now she fights with the Arrows, never forgetting how she chose to hunt, rather than be hunted.<br /> <b>Regain Mana or Willpower:</b> When Nadia witnesses a person act ruthlessly without provocation or resorts to violience similarly unprovoked.<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower:</b> When Nadia carries out a needlessly violent attack on an enemy, or one that invites similarly violent reprisal.<br /> <b>Use As Yantra:</b> When making a preemptive strike against an enemy.<br /> <br /> <b>Equivalent Exchange:</b> Scott was your average conman, trying to get something for nothing, any way he could. This was adventurous work, no doubt, but it left him with fewer friends than enemies. He was cornered by said enemies, but thankfully he'd managed to scrape together enough cash to barely pay them off before the very literal deadline. What he saw when he opened his motel room door was not at all what he expected, though. He thought he was going to meet a couple of guys, maybe wearing tracksuits, but standing before him were two shades, faceless shadows with grasping hands and rasping, ragged breathing. One held out a hand, silently demanding the money, which Scott silently gave. The shade nodded appreciatively, and turned to leave. Its associate lingered for a moment, before grabbing Scott's empty, out-stretched hand. Scott stifled a scream, and the specter silently placed a single lead coin in his hand. Nothing's free, after all, not even money.<br /> <b>Regain Mana or Willpower:</b> When Scott witnesses two or more people make exchanges in good faith and on equal terms or takes part in such an exchange.<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower:</b> When conducting business fairly and honestly with those who will probably abuse his fairness.<br /> <b>Use As Yantra:</b> When facilitating trades and exchanges.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Lie: Comforting Delusions</b></span><br /> <br /> Amazing as the Supernal World may be, it's also terrifying. The sheer magnitude of the burden the Awakening places on a Mage is staggering, and it's only natural to seek some comfort in the familiarity of the Fallen World. A Mage's personal Lie is something they know isn't true, but takes some of the edge off of Awakened life. Some call it a crutch, others call it the vestiges of the &quot;Big&quot; Lie still sticking to the Mage's Soul, and others just consider it a part of their soul like anything else.<br /> <br /> When a Mage indulges in her Lie, she regains a point of Willpower, relieving the stress of Awakened life by turning inward from it.<br /> <br /> When a Mage indulges her Lie at the expense of her Obsessions or well-being, she can either fully refresh her Willpower, using her Lie as a defense mechanism, or she can scour a Paradox Condition from her Pattern without suffering Lethal damage, as she forces the Paradox out with willful ignorance.<br /> <br /> When rolling for a Breaking Point resulting from indulging the Lie, the roll is penalized as if the Mage was acting on her Vice.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Lies:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>It'll All Be Back to Normal Soon:</b> Roger grew up on all those hokey sitcoms where everything ends up exactly how it always was, just in time for next week's episode. Everybody knows that kind of shit doesn't happen in real life, but it's enough to keep Roger from panicking.<br /> <b>Regain Willpower:</b> Whenever Roger refuses to accept a change in his life.<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower or Scour Paradox:</b> When Roger completely fails to act, hoping the problem will go away.<br /> <br /> <b>Everything Happens For a Reason:</b> All Zach could see after Awakening were the shadows moving, everywhere. He tries to act like they're all acting according to a plan, that there's a reason for everything instead of the random series of terrifying events that appears to play out each day for him.<br /> <b>Regain Willpower:</b> When Zach tries to connect unrelated events.<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower or Scour Paradox:</b> When Zach puts himself in danger by acting based on false connections.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 11-10-2016, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T23:31:19-07:00","id":998632,"title":"","content":"I LOVE this: from now this will be &quot;canon&quot; at my tables !!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T04:07:57-07:00","id":998686,"title":"","content":"Didn't I see this hack somewhere on the forum before? It's great but I think I remember it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:51:03-07:00","id":998736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/998602-mage-virtue-vice-replacements?p=998632#post998632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I LOVE this: from now this will be &quot;canon&quot; at my tables !!</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/998602-mage-virtue-vice-replacements?p=998686#post998686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't I see this hack somewhere on the forum before? It's great but I think I remember it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somebody talked about the concept, I think, but I don't recall seeing it fully written out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:23:11-07:00","id":998776,"title":"","content":"I appreciate and applaud your thinking but I'm not sure I like it, myself. A part of that is keyed to the idea that I like the Awakened as humans and feel the presence of Obsessions does enough to drive them to extreme acts. The other half, though, is that I don't think there's anything that can fall into the Lie slot that doesn't also fall into the Truth slot, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> For example, you have Everything Happens For a Reason, and that idea is ostensibly True. Fate is a thing that exists, after all, and the concept is a core conceit of mystagogues, who believe that the Mysteries themselves dance to a grand cosmic plan. Seers, likewise, see the hand of the Exarchs in the Fallen World; binding lines of power into the bars of a grand cosmic prison. It'll All Be Back To Normal Soon fits with the very concept of Thyrsus Gnosis which sees the grand details as largely fixed and unchanging and the small ones being in flux ostensibly a part of the Lie.<br /> <br /> Contrariwise, Hunt or Be Hunted is something that is the foundation stone of the Raptorial Seal; one of the very Exarchs who enforces the Lie. The idea that there is only victimization or victimhood is an idea soundly challenged by the Silver Ladder and Mysterium (and tacitly accepted by the Adamantine Arrow).<br /> <br /> If these are features, not bugs, then carry on. I might simply be misunderstanding and the intent could be that, rather than lining up with actual Supernal Truth or Fallen Lie, but rather being ways the Mage is able to approach the Supernal or retreats into the Lie. If that's the case, they become a slightly more complex Virtue and Vice which, for the Awakened, I think might be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:54:15-07:00","id":998784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/998602-mage-virtue-vice-replacements?p=998776#post998776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate and applaud your thinking but I'm not sure I like it, myself. A part of that is keyed to the idea that I like the Awakened as humans and feel the presence of Obsessions does enough to drive them to extreme acts. The other half, though, is that I don't think there's anything that can fall into the Lie slot that doesn't also fall into the Truth slot, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> If these are features, not bugs, then carry on. I might simply be misunderstanding and the intent could be that, rather than lining up with actual Supernal Truth or Fallen Lie, but rather being ways the Mage is able to approach the Supernal or retreats into the Lie. If that's the case, they become a slightly more complex Virtue and Vice which, for the Awakened, I think might be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are indeed features rather than bugs. I like the possibility of something being a Truth for one Mage and a Lie for others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:21:00-08:00","id":999485,"title":"","content":"The issue here is... who decides what's a truth and what's a lie? All of those statements are subjective. Try telling an Acanthus that not everything happens for a reason and they'll look at you like the town's idiot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T17:56:41-08:00","id":999505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/998602-mage-virtue-vice-replacements?p=999485#post999485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue here is... who decides what's a truth and what's a lie? All of those statements are subjective. Try telling an Acanthus that not everything happens for a reason and they'll look at you like the town's idiot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's kind of intentional. Any coherent thing you could say could be &quot;True&quot; or &quot;False&quot; in this context. A Mage's Truth doesn't give them power because it's true everywhere and at all times, but because it's True for them. The Mage's Lie is False for them because it stands counter to the Supernal symbolism that makes up their Gnosis.<br /> <br /> So you could have an Mage who has &quot;People are Fundamentally Selfish&quot; as a Truth, because it's resonant with <i>their</i> Gnosis, and you could have another Mage who has &quot;People are Fundamentally Altruistic&quot; as a Truth, and be just as right <i>for their own soul</i>. And I'm sure that Acanthus could say any number of things that would make any number of other Magi look at them like the town's idiot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T18:34:45-08:00","id":999518,"title":"","content":"I mean, isn't it much the same way that some virtues can be vices and vice versa (pun not intended)? Take &quot;Ambition&quot; for example, which I believe is actually a listed example of a trait that can be either a virtue or a vice. It all depends on its relation to the character in question...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T01:49:08-08:00","id":999621,"title":"","content":"People generally say 'everything happens for a reason' to try and reconcile themselves to horrible things happening to them.<br /> <br /> An Acanthus might agree in a literal sense, but they're not using it as a defence mechanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T18:32:30-08:00","id":1000570,"title":"","content":"Interesting enough, maybe I'll use it on some game. Maybe I'll hack it a little to resemble a little more Virtue/Vice, so it don't get &quot;too much&quot; far from the human side, but still makes for a touch of the Supernal in their psyches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:02:10-08:00","id":1001048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/998602-mage-virtue-vice-replacements?p=998686#post998686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't I see this hack somewhere on the forum before? It's great but I think I remember it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You did, I presented a similar hack before, though it kinda died since I didn't make any examples. That said, my own concept was a bit different. Both Truth and Lie were a combination of a Virtue and a Vice, Truth's Virtue was the mage's connection to the Supernal, the Vice represented their detachment to humanity. Lie's Virtue and Vice was the complete reverse. To be honest, I actually like this more subjective concept better.<br /> <br /> Couple problems I have with the mechanics, though: 1) Truth only gives 1 Mana back. I know it's only an option, but seriously, who's gonna pick it unless they have no WP to regain? 2) Truth seems easy to fulfill, but Lie requires some substantial sacrifice, shouldn't it be the other way round?<br /> <br /> I've got some suggestions. Operate Truth and Lie much like Mask and Dirge or Blood and Bone, where there are two ways to regain WP with each, only for Truth and Lie there's an alternate benefit to each one: When fulfilling Truth in a significant manner, regain WP, but seeing the Truth reflected or fulfilling it in a minor way, regain 1 Mana instead of 1 WP. Likewise with Lie, fulfilling it in a minor way regains 1 WP, but doing so at the expense of Obsessions or something equally significant allows you to resolve a Paradox Condition.<br /> <br /> Just throwing some ideas around. Little side note, diggin' the Equivalent Exchange Truth, Ed and Al would totally have that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:07:47-08:00","id":1001049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/998602-mage-virtue-vice-replacements?p=1001048#post1001048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You did, I presented a similar hack before, though it kinda died since I didn't make any examples. That said, my own concept was a bit different. Both Truth and Lie were a combination of a Virtue and a Vice, Truth's Virtue was the mage's connection to the Supernal, the Vice represented their detachment to humanity. Lie's Virtue and Vice was the complete reverse. To be honest, I actually like this more subjective concept better.<br /> <br /> Couple problems I have with the mechanics, though: 1) Truth only gives 1 Mana back. I know it's only an option, but seriously, who's gonna pick it unless they have no WP to regain? 2) Truth seems easy to fulfill, but Lie requires some substantial sacrifice, shouldn't it be the other way round?<br /> <br /> I've got some suggestions. Operate Truth and Lie much like Mask and Dirge or Blood and Bone, where there are two ways to regain WP with each, only for Truth and Lie there's an alternate benefit to each one: When fulfilling Truth in a significant manner, regain WP, but seeing the Truth reflected or fulfilling it in a minor way, regain 1 Mana instead of 1 WP. Likewise with Lie, fulfilling it in a minor way regains 1 WP, but doing so at the expense of Obsessions or something equally significant allows you to resolve a Paradox Condition.<br /> <br /> Just throwing some ideas around. Little side note, diggin' the Equivalent Exchange Truth, Ed and Al would totally have that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T06:04:12-08:00","id":1001330,"title":"","content":"We're missing a &quot;regain all willpower&quot; condition. That's kinda useful for a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:01:40-08:00","id":1001476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/998602-mage-virtue-vice-replacements?p=998776#post998776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate and applaud your thinking but I'm not sure I like it, myself. A part of that is keyed to the idea that I like the Awakened as humans and feel the presence of Obsessions does enough to drive them to extreme acts. The other half, though, is that I don't think there's anything that can fall into the Lie slot that doesn't also fall into the Truth slot, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> For example, you have Everything Happens For a Reason, and that idea is ostensibly True. Fate is a thing that exists, after all, and the concept is a core conceit of mystagogues, who believe that the Mysteries themselves dance to a grand cosmic plan. Seers, likewise, see the hand of the Exarchs in the Fallen World; binding lines of power into the bars of a grand cosmic prison. It'll All Be Back To Normal Soon fits with the very concept of Thyrsus Gnosis which sees the grand details as largely fixed and unchanging and the small ones being in flux ostensibly a part of the Lie.<br /> <br /> Contrariwise, Hunt or Be Hunted is something that is the foundation stone of the Raptorial Seal; one of the very Exarchs who enforces the Lie. The idea that there is only victimization or victimhood is an idea soundly challenged by the Silver Ladder and Mysterium (and tacitly accepted by the Adamantine Arrow).<br /> <br /> If these are features, not bugs, then carry on. I might simply be misunderstanding and the intent could be that, rather than lining up with actual Supernal Truth or Fallen Lie, but rather being ways the Mage is able to approach the Supernal or retreats into the Lie. If that's the case, they become a slightly more complex Virtue and Vice which, for the Awakened, I think might be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems true of many virtues and vices, where they are features as well, the Ambitious falling in either category comes to mind. I see the same thing as you, but think it is meant as a feature of the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:37:37-08:00","id":1001497,"title":"","content":"I like this hack a lot, it's a more elegant take on one of my own. I believe I will implement it in future Mage games. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T19:07:51-08:00","id":1002744,"title":"","content":"I like this hack as well. I liked it so much that I came up with a Truth and a Lie. What do you think, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a>?<br /> <br /> <b>All Choices Matter<br /> Regain Mana or Willpower:</b> When you explain to someone how their current course of action might significantly impact their life<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower:</b> When you arrange events so that a seemingly inconsequential choice significantly alters someone\u2019s destiny and they notice it<br /> <b>Use As Yantra:</b> When trying to make sure someone considers all options before making an important decision<br /> <br /> <b>Pleasure Is Everything</b><br /> <b>Regain Willpower:</b> When you put aside a responsibility to pursue the next thrill<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower or Scour Paradox:</b> When you damage your health or reputation by succumbing to extreme hedonism<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T04:57:11-08:00","id":1002834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/998602-mage-virtue-vice-replacements?p=1002744#post1002744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this hack as well. I liked it so much that I came up with a Truth and a Lie. What do you think, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4488_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4488\" data-vbnamecard=\"4488\">malonkey1</a>?<br /> <br /> <b>All Choices Matter<br /> Regain Mana or Willpower:</b> When you explain to someone how their current course of action might significantly impact their life<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower:</b> When you arrange events so that a seemingly inconsequential choice significantly alters someone\u2019s destiny and they notice it<br /> <b>Use As Yantra:</b> When trying to make sure someone considers all options before making an important decision<br /> <br /> <b>Pleasure Is Everything</b><br /> <b>Regain Willpower:</b> When you put aside a responsibility to pursue the next thrill<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower or Scour Paradox:</b> When you damage your health or reputation by succumbing to extreme hedonism</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've got the idea pretty well. Here's those two same concepts switched, just for fun:<br /> <br /> <b>All Choices Matter</b> (as a Lie)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> You don't believe in fate and destiny, which is a little odd since you personally know people who manipulate them regularly. You are careful with every choice you make, even ones that aren't really that important, and when you do make choices, you tend to be very stubborn with regards to what others call &quot;inevitable&quot;.<br /> <b>Regain Willpower:</b> When you fail to make a snap decision due to indecisiveness.<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower or Scour Paradox:</b> When you place yourself and others in unnecessary danger to prevent the inevitable.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Pleasure is Everything</b> (as a Truth)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> All a person is is what they feel. Given this, doesn't it make sense to make sure everybody feels good whenever possible?<br /> <b>Regain Mana or Willpower:</b> When you take part in merrymaking and hedonism.<br /> <b>Regain All Willpower:</b> When you place your physical or emotional well-being in jeopardy to keep others from suffering.<br /> <b>Use as Yantra:</b> When attempting to invoke feelings of pleasure and joy.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}